e, works offline once weights are on disk; requires an M5 Mac with 64GB RAM at launch.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-25\",\n    \"category\": \"IDE-integrated coding agent (on-device)\",\n    \"sources\": [\"JetBrains blog\", \"Hacker News\", \"techstrong.ai\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Opslane\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/opslane/opslane\",\n    \"description\": \"Open-source, self-hostable (Docker Compose) agent that watches user sessions — rrweb recordings, rage clicks, dead clicks, abandoned forms — finds the bugs that actually matter, investigates them, and only opens a PR when it can verify the fix. Ships an MCP server so developers can query it from Claude Code.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-27\",\n    \"category\": \"workflow agent (bug triage & fix)\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Show HN\", \"GitHub\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"The end-user recording aspect makes this an absolute non-starter for me.\",\n      \"Most people won't file bugs, they'll just churn.\",\n      \"PostHog already has similar 'Scouts' agents that review event data and open PRs.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Ambient Context\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/dragthelake/ambient-context\",\n    \"description\": \"macOS menu-bar app that captures focused-window text via the Accessibility API and writes it to daily Markdown files — no screenshots, no OCR. Aimed at giving coding agents like Claude Code persistent context about what you actually worked on; includes an AGENTS.md format guide for building project memory.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-25\",\n    \"category\": \"agent memory (screen-to-Markdown)\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Show HN\", \"GitHub\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"Point Claude Code (or anything with file access) at the folder to ask what you worked on.\",\n      \"A screenshot-to-OCR loop definitely is more expensive than the accessibility API.\",\n      \"most apps just aren't wired up right — per-app profiles are needed.\",\n      \"Fundamentally the wrong approach; structured digital footprints (git commits, Slack, tickets) already capture your work.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"SlideOps\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/glukicov/slideops\",\n    \"description\": \"Open-source Claude Code plugin (also runs in Copilot CLI) that generates engineering slides/updates directly from a repository and automatically flags when they drift from the code. Turns 'stale deck' maintenance into a checked-in, testable workflow.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-31\",\n    \"category\": \"Claude Code plugin (docs drift detection)\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Show HN\", \"GitHub\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"Would be great to generalize to documentation in general, not just slides.\",\n      \"Docs drift is a problem LLMs could uniquely solve — models don't mind updating docs.\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"49 IDE\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/alpbahadur/49-IDE\",\n    \"description\": \"Open-source '2D canvas' agentic IDE: an infinite zoomable canvas holding AI coding agents in native CLIs (Claude Code, Codex), live tmux terminals, git graph, Monaco editor, and notes in one unified space. Self-host locally with 49ctl and reach it from laptop, tablet, or phone; BSL 1.1, free for individuals and small teams.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-31\",\n    \"category\": \"AI IDE (2D canvas for agents)\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Show HN\", \"GitHub\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Cover\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/DavidCarliez/cover\",\n    \"description\": \"Open-source guardrail that keeps private data, internal infrastructure, and secrets out of cloud coding agents without breaking your existing workflow — a local filtering layer for Claude Code/Codex-style cloud agents.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-21\",\n    \"category\": \"security layer for cloud coding agents\",\n    \"sources\": [\"GitHub\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Vicoa\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/vicoa-ai/vicoa\",\n    \"description\": \"Open-source, self-hostable 'agentic development environment' for running a team of coding agents from any device — desktop, mobile, or VPS. Keeps agent sessions reachable and steerable when you step away from the keyboard.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-28\",\n    \"category\": \"agentic dev environment (self-hosted)\",\n    \"sources\": [\"GitHub\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Polign Edge Agent Memory\",\n    \"url\": \"https://polign.com/blog-edge-agent-memory\",\n    \"description\": \"Lightweight, stateless database for agent memory designed to run at the edge on tiny resources (author reports ~37MiB RSS while serving 12.5M passages), with cold-data caching and a zero-outbound-calls binary. Closed-source for now, which sparked debate on HN.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-26\",\n    \"category\": \"agent memory database\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Show HN\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": [\n      \"I've vibe coded the same exact thing multiple times.\",\n      \"litestream with sqlite vector based design would be more apt for someone.\",\n      \"I get the closed source open binary approach — I would test it if I would be in need!\"\n    ]\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Devx\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/apvcode/Termux-Dev\",\n    \"description\": \"Autonomous AI coding agent built to run on Android Termux as well as desktop — repo-aware, can run commands and manage tasks from a phone, bringing Claude Code-style workflows to mobile.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-26\",\n    \"category\": \"coding agent (Termux/desktop)\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Show HN\", \"GitHub\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"VT Code\",\n    \"url\": \"https://vinhnx.github.io/VTCode/\",\n    \"description\": \"Terminal-native coding agent with a human-reviewed WebMCP editing flow, so every agent-driven code change passes through an explicit review step — a repo-aware CLI agent in the Claude Code/Codex mold.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-29\",\n    \"category\": \"AI coding CLI\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Show HN\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Intent\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.intentapp.dev/\",\n    \"description\": \"A high-scale coding agent orchestrator that just went open source: coordinates many coding-agent runs across repos and machines instead of a single chat session.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-31\",\n    \"category\": \"coding agent orchestrator\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Hacker News\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Open Session\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.opensession.com/\",\n    \"description\": \"Open-source, self-hostable cloud agent orchestrator built by the founders of Tella (YC S20): spin up, run, and review coding-agent sessions in the cloud with team collaboration built in.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-27\",\n    \"category\": \"agent orchestrator (self-hosted)\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Show HN\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Zuse\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.zuse.sh/\",\n    \"description\": \"Open-source workspace for coding agents where a single agent coordinates up to 20 Linear issues in parallel Git worktrees — ticket-to-PR orchestration across many branches at once.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-23\",\n    \"category\": \"workflow agent (issues + worktrees)\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Show HN\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"ThinkRail\",\n    \"url\": \"https://thinkrail.ai/blog/introducing-thinkrail/\",\n    \"description\": \"A web-based GUI for the Pi coding agent, incubated inside JetBrains: browse sessions, review diffs, and manage agent runs from the browser instead of the terminal.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-25\",\n    \"category\": \"web GUI for coding agent\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Hacker News\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Itsuki\",\n    \"url\": \"https://itsuki.app/\",\n    \"description\": \"Shared memory layer that lets Claude Code, Cursor, and 24+ other AI coding tools read and write one common memory store, keeping context consistent across sessions and machines.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-29\",\n    \"category\": \"cross-tool agent memory\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Show HN\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"OpenContext\",\n    \"url\": \"https://www.opencntx.dev/\",\n    \"description\": \"Persistent, project-local memory for AI coding agents exposed via MCP — keeps codebase context across sessions locally instead of shipping it to a cloud memory service.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-29\",\n    \"category\": \"project-local agent memory (MCP)\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Hacker News\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Argus\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/argus-testing/argus\",\n    \"description\": \"Open-source AI agents specialized in testing web applications — generating and running end-to-end tests against your app rather than writing feature code.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-28\",\n    \"category\": \"AI testing agents\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Show HN\", \"GitHub\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": []\n  },\n  {\n    \"name\": \"Revue\",\n    \"url\": \"https://github.com/mtford90/revue\",\n    \"description\": \"Terminal TUI for reviewing large code changes — including big agent-generated diffs — one 'chapter' at a time instead of scrolling a single giant diff.\",\n    \"release_date\": \"2026-08-31\",\n    \"category\": \"terminal code review TUI\",\n    \"sources\": [\"Show HN\", \"GitHub\"],\n    \"community_quotes\": []\n  }\n]\n",
