    "content": "<!DOCTYPE html>\n<html lang=\"en\">\n<head>\n<meta charset=\"UTF-8\">\n<meta name=\"viewport\" content=\"width=device-width, initial-scale=1.0\">\n<meta name=\"description\" content=\"Agent Daily — agentic coding research report for 2026-08-31: 20 new products, 16 whitelist updates, 38 technical insights.\">\n<title>Agentic Coding Research Report — 2026-08-31</title>\n<style>\n  * { box-sizing: border-box; margin: 0; padding: 0; }\n\n  :root {\n    --bg: #f6f6ef;\n    --card: #fffef7;\n    --text: #000000;\n    --muted: #828282;\n    --accent: #ff6600;\n    --border: #d4d4d4;\n  }\n\n  html { scroll-behavior: smooth; }\n\n  body {\n    background: var(--bg);\n    color: var(--text);\n    font-family: Verdana, Geneva, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 13px;\n    line-height: 1.45;\n  }\n\n  a { color: var(--text); }\n  a:focus-visible { outline: 2px solid var(--accent); outline-offset: 1px; }\n\n  .skip-link {\n    position: absolute; left: -9999px; top: 0;\n    background: var(--accent); color: #fff; padding: 6px 12px; z-index: 99;\n    font-size: 12px; text-decoration: none;\n  }\n  .skip-link:focus { left: 8px; top: 8px; }\n\n  /* ---------- Top bar (HN-style) ---------- */\n  .topbar {\n    background: var(--accent);\n    padding: 6px 14px;\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: center;\n    gap: 16px;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n  }\n  .brand {\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    font-size: 15px;\n    color: #000;\n    text-decoration: none;\n    letter-spacing: .01em;\n  }\n  .brand:hover { text-decoration: underline; }\n  .topbar nav { display: flex; gap: 10px; }\n  .topbar nav a {\n    color: #000;\n    font-size: 12px;\n    text-decoration: none;\n  }\n  .topbar nav a:hover { color: #fff; text-decoration: underline; }\n  .topbar .edition {\n    margin-left: auto;\n    font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n    font-size: 12px;\n    color: #000;\n  }\n\n  .print-header { display: none; }\n\n  /* ---------- Hero ---------- */\n  .hero { max-width: 1480px; margin: 0 auto; padding: 16px 16px 2px; }\n  .hero h1 {\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 21px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n  }\n  .hero h1 .accent { color: var(--accent); }\n  .hero .tagline { margin-top: 3px; color: var(--muted); font-size: 12px; }\n  .stats { display: flex; gap: 8px; flex-wrap: wrap; margin-top: 9px; }\n  .chip {\n    font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n    font-size: 11px;\n    border: 1px solid var(--border);\n    background: var(--card);\n    color: #555;\n    padding: 2px 9px;\n    border-radius: 10px;\n  }\n  .chip b { color: var(--accent); font-weight: 700; }\n\n  /* ---------- Layout ---------- */\n  .layout {\n    max-width: 1480px;\n    margin: 14px auto 0;\n    padding: 0 16px 28px;\n    display: grid;\n    grid-template-columns: 40fr 35fr 25fr;\n    gap: 16px;\n    align-items: start;\n  }\n  .col { min-width: 0; }\n\n  .col-head {\n    position: sticky;\n    top: 0;\n    z-index: 5;\n    background: var(--bg);\n    padding: 8px 2px 7px;\n    border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: baseline;\n    gap: 8px;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n  }\n  .col-head h2 {\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 13px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    letter-spacing: .07em;\n  }\n  .col-head h2 a { text-decoration: none; }\n  .col-head h2 a:hover { color: var(--accent); }\n  .col-head .count {\n    font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n    font-size: 11px;\n    color: var(--muted);\n  }\n\n  .cards { display: flex; flex-direction: column; gap: 10px; margin-top: 11px; }\n\n  /* ---------- Cards ---------- */\n  .card {\n    background: var(--card);\n    border: 1px solid var(--border);\n    border-radius: 3px;\n    padding: 9px 11px;\n    transition: border-color .12s ease, box-shadow .12s ease;\n  }\n  .card:hover { border-color: var(--accent); box-shadow: 0 1px 3px rgba(0,0,0,.08); }\n\n  .card-head {\n    display: flex;\n    align-items: baseline;\n    gap: 7px;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n  }\n  .idx {\n    font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n    font-size: 10.5px;\n    color: var(--muted);\n    min-width: 18px;\n    text-align: right;\n  }\n  .card h3 {\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-size: 13.5px;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    line-height: 1.3;\n    flex: 1 1 auto;\n  }\n  .card h3 a { text-decoration: none; color: var(--text); }\n  .card h3 a:hover { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; }\n\n  .type {\n    font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n    font-size: 9.5px;\n    text-transform: uppercase;\n    letter-spacing: .05em;\n    padding: 1px 6px;\n    border-radius: 2px;\n    white-space: nowrap;\n  }\n  .t-release      { background: #ececec; color: #444; }\n  .t-feature      { background: #ffe8d4; color: #c14e00; }\n  .t-announcement { background: #e8eef7; color: #39597f; }\n  .t-opinion      { background: #fff0e0; color: #b35a00; }\n  .t-discussion   { background: #ececec; color: #444; }\n  .t-technical    { background: #e8eef7; color: #39597f; }\n  .t-tutorial     { background: #e9f3e6; color: #3c6e33; }\n  .t-paper        { background: #f1e8f7; color: #6a3d8f; }\n\n  .date {\n    font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n    font-size: 10.5px;\n    color: var(--muted);\n    white-space: nowrap;\n  }\n\n  .subtitle {\n    margin-top: 4px;\n    font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n    font-size: 11px;\n    color: #555;\n  }\n  .desc { margin-top: 4px; font-size: 12px; color: #333; }\n  .desc code {\n    font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n    font-size: 11px;\n    background: #f0f0e6;\n    border: 1px solid #e2e2d6;\n    border-radius: 2px;\n    padding: 0 3px;\n  }\n\n  .meta {\n    margin-top: 7px;\n    display: flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    gap: 6px 10px;\n    align-items: center;\n    font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n    font-size: 10.5px;\n    color: var(--muted);\n  }\n  .tag {\n    border: 1px solid #e2e2da;\n    background: #f4f4ea;\n    padding: 1px 7px;\n    border-radius: 9px;\n    color: #666;\n    font-size: 10px;\n  }\n  .src { color: var(--muted); }\n  .notes-link {\n    color: var(--accent);\n    text-decoration: none;\n    font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n    font-size: 10.5px;\n  }\n  .notes-link:hover { text-decoration: underline; }\n\n  .quote {\n    margin-top: 7px;\n    border-left: 3px solid var(--accent);\n    background: #fbfbf2;\n    padding: 4px 9px;\n    font-size: 11px;\n    color: #555;\n    font-style: italic;\n  }\n  .quote .qsrc {\n    font-style: normal;\n    color: #999;\n    font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n    font-size: 9.5px;\n    white-space: nowrap;\n  }\n\n  /* Insights (compact) */\n  .insight { padding: 8px 10px; }\n  .insight .card-head { justify-content: space-between; }\n  .insight h3 { font-size: 12.5px; }\n  .insight .desc { font-size: 11.5px; color: #444; }\n  .author {\n    margin-top: 3px;\n    font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n    font-size: 10.5px;\n    color: var(--muted);\n  }\n\n  .col-foot {\n    margin-top: 12px;\n    font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace;\n    font-size: 10.5px;\n    color: var(--muted);\n    text-align: center;\n  }\n\n  /* ---------- Footer ---------- */\n  footer {\n    border-top: 2px solid var(--accent);\n    background: #efefe7;\n  }\n  .foot-inner {\n    max-width: 1480px;\n    margin: 0 auto;\n    padding: 14px 16px 20px;\n    display: flex;\n    flex-wrap: wrap;\n    gap: 8px 18px;\n    align-items: baseline;\n    font-size: 11.5px;\n    color: var(--muted);\n  }\n  .foot-inner .fbrand {\n    font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n    font-weight: 700;\n    color: var(--text);\n  }\n  .foot-inner nav { display: flex; gap: 12px; }\n  .foot-inner nav a { color: var(--muted); text-decoration: none; }\n  .foot-inner nav a:hover { color: var(--accent); text-decoration: underline; }\n  .foot-inner .fmuted { margin-left: auto; font-family: Monaco, Consolas, monospace; font-size: 10.5px; }\n\n  section { scroll-margin-top: 8px; }\n\n  /* ---------- Responsive ---------- */\n  @media (max-width: 1150px) {\n    .layout {\n      grid-template-columns: 1fr 1fr;\n      grid-template-areas:\n        \"a a\"\n        \"b c\";\n    }\n    .col-products { grid-area: a; }\n    .col-updates  { grid-area: b; }\n    .col-insights { grid-area: c; }\n  }\n  @media (max-width: 720px) {\n    .layout { grid-template-columns: 1fr; grid-template-areas: \"a\" \"b\" \"c\"; }\n    .hero h1 { font-size: 18px; }\n    .topbar .edition { margin-left: 0; width: 100%; }\n    .col-head { position: static; }\n  }\n\n  /* ---------- Print ---------- */\n  @media print {\n    body { background: #fff; font-size: 10pt; }\n    .topbar, .skip-link { background: none; }\n    .topbar nav, .topbar .edition { display: none; }\n    .print-header {\n      display: block;\n      font-family: Arial, Helvetica, sans-serif;\n      font-weight: 700;\n      font-size: 13pt;\n      padding: 4px 0;\n      border-bottom: 2px solid var(--accent);\n      margin: 0 0 10px;\n    }\n    .layout { display: block; max-width: none; padding: 0; }\n    .col + .col { margin-top: 20px; }\n    .col-head { position: static; }\n    .card { border: 1px solid #bbb; box-shadow: none; break-inside: avoid; }\n    .card:hover { box-shadow: none; border-color: #bbb; }\n    .chip { background: #fff; }\n    a { color: #000; }\n    .notes-link::after { content: \" (\" attr(href) \")\"; font-size: 8pt; color: #555; }\n  }\n</style>\n</head>\n<body id=\"top\">\n<a class=\"skip-link\" href=\"#main\">Skip to content</a>\n\n<div class=\"topbar\" role=\"banner\">\n  <a class=\"brand\" href=\"#top\">Agent Daily</a>\n  <nav aria-label=\"Sections\">\n    <a href=\"#new-products\">new products</a>\n    <a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">updates</a>\n    <a href=\"#technical-insights\">insights</a>\n  </nav>\n  <span class=\"edition\">2026-08-31</span>\n</div>\n\n<div class=\"print-header\">Agent Daily — Agentic Coding Research Report — 2026-08-31</div>\n\n<header class=\"hero\">\n  <h1>Agentic Coding Research Report <span class=\"accent\">/ 2026-08-31</span></h1>\n  <p class=\"tagline\">Daily digest of the agentic coding ecosystem — new tools, shipping cadence from the major players, and what the community is arguing about.</p>\n  <div class=\"stats\" aria-label=\"Report statistics\">\n    <span class=\"chip\"><b>20</b> new products</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\"><b>16</b> whitelist updates</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\"><b>38</b> technical insights</span>\n    <span class=\"chip\"><b>74</b> items total</span>\n  </div>\n</header>\n\n<main id=\"main\" class=\"layout\">\n\n  <!-- ================= LEFT: NEW PRODUCTS (40%) ================= -->\n  <section id=\"new-products\" class=\"col col-products\" aria-labelledby=\"h2-products\">\n    <div class=\"col-head\">\n      <h2 id=\"h2-products\"><a href=\"#new-products\">New Products</a></h2>\n      <span class=\"count\">20 items</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"cards\">\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">1</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/proliferate-ai/proliferate\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Proliferate</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-21</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Self-hostable AI IDE from a YC S25 founder that unifies Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode, Cursor and Grok in one workspace — per-harness native auth/inference, parent agents spawning subagents, and 'workflows': chained agent sessions with human approval gates.</p>\n        <blockquote class=\"quote\">\"ooo, nice Workflows feature you got there.\" <span class=\"qsrc\">HN</span></blockquote>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">self-hostable AI IDE</span><span class=\"src\">Show HN · GitHub</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">2</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/useagenthq/useagent\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">UseAgent</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-29</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Open-source 'AI coworker' platform wrapping Claude Code, Codex, OpenCode and Pi behind one interface — each run gets an isolated cloud sandbox (terminal, browser, noVNC) with Slack-native approvals, team memory and versioned skills, returning tested PRs. AGPL-3.0, alpha.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">coding-agent platform</span><span class=\"src\">GitHub</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">3</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://blog.jetbrains.com/junie/2026/08/junie-local-launch/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Junie Local</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-25</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">JetBrains' first fully on-device coding agent: type /local to download a JetBrains-tuned Qwen3.6-27B (4-bit, ~20GB) and Junie runs entirely on your Mac — no cloud, subscription or credits. Free and offline-capable; requires an M5 Mac with 64GB RAM at launch.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">on-device coding agent</span><span class=\"src\">JetBrains blog · HN · techstrong.ai</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">4</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/opslane/opslane\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Opslane</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-27</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Self-hostable agent (Docker Compose) that watches user sessions — rrweb recordings, rage clicks, dead clicks, abandoned forms — finds the bugs that actually matter, investigates them, and only opens a PR when it can verify the fix. Ships an MCP server for Claude Code.</p>\n        <blockquote class=\"quote\">\"The end-user recording aspect makes this an absolute non-starter for me.\" <span class=\"qsrc\">HN</span></blockquote>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">bug triage &amp; fix agent</span><span class=\"src\">Show HN · GitHub</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">5</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/dragthelake/ambient-context\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Ambient Context</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-25</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">macOS menu-bar app that captures focused-window text via the Accessibility API into daily Markdown files — no screenshots, no OCR — giving coding agents like Claude Code persistent context on what you actually worked on. Includes an AGENTS.md format guide for project memory.</p>\n        <blockquote class=\"quote\">\"Point Claude Code (or anything with file access) at the folder to ask what you worked on.\" <span class=\"qsrc\">HN</span></blockquote>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">agent memory (screen-to-Markdown)</span><span class=\"src\">Show HN · GitHub</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">6</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/glukicov/slideops\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">SlideOps</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-31</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Claude Code plugin (also runs in Copilot CLI) that generates engineering slides and updates straight from a repository and automatically flags when they drift from the code — 'stale deck' maintenance becomes a checked-in, testable workflow.</p>\n        <blockquote class=\"quote\">\"Docs drift is a problem LLMs could uniquely solve — models don't mind updating docs.\" <span class=\"qsrc\">HN</span></blockquote>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">docs drift detection</span><span class=\"src\">Show HN · GitHub</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">7</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/alpbahadur/49-IDE\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">49 IDE</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-31</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">'2D canvas' agentic IDE: an infinite zoomable canvas holding AI coding agents in native CLIs (Claude Code, Codex), live tmux terminals, a git graph, Monaco editor and notes in one space. Self-host locally with 49ctl and reach it from laptop, tablet or phone. BSL 1.1.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">AI IDE (2D canvas)</span><span class=\"src\">Show HN · GitHub</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">8</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/DavidCarliez/cover\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cover</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-21</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Open-source guardrail that keeps private data, internal infrastructure and secrets out of cloud coding agents without breaking your existing workflow — a local filtering layer for Claude Code/Codex-style cloud agents.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">security layer</span><span class=\"src\">GitHub</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">9</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/vicoa-ai/vicoa\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Vicoa</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-28</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Self-hostable 'agentic development environment' for running a team of coding agents from any device — desktop, mobile or VPS — keeping agent sessions reachable and steerable when you step away from the keyboard.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">agentic dev environment</span><span class=\"src\">GitHub</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">10</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://polign.com/blog-edge-agent-memory\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Polign Edge Agent Memory</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-26</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Lightweight, stateless database for agent memory designed for the edge — author reports ~37MiB RSS while serving 12.5M passages — with cold-data caching and a zero-outbound-calls binary. Closed-source, which sparked debate on HN.</p>\n        <blockquote class=\"quote\">\"I've vibe coded the same exact thing multiple times.\" <span class=\"qsrc\">HN</span></blockquote>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">agent memory database</span><span class=\"src\">Show HN</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">11</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/apvcode/Termux-Dev\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Devx</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-26</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Autonomous coding agent built to run on Android Termux as well as desktop — repo-aware, runs commands and manages tasks from a phone, bringing Claude Code-style workflows to mobile.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">coding agent (Termux)</span><span class=\"src\">Show HN · GitHub</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">12</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://vinhnx.github.io/VTCode/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">VT Code</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-29</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Terminal-native coding agent with a human-reviewed WebMCP editing flow, so every agent-driven code change passes through an explicit review step — a repo-aware CLI agent in the Claude Code/Codex mold.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">AI coding CLI</span><span class=\"src\">Show HN</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">13</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://www.intentapp.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Intent</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-31</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">High-scale coding-agent orchestrator that just went open source — coordinates many coding-agent runs across repos and machines instead of a single chat session.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">agent orchestrator</span><span class=\"src\">Hacker News</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">14</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://www.opensession.com/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Open Session</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-27</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Self-hostable cloud agent orchestrator built by the founders of Tella (YC S20): spin up, run and review coding-agent sessions in the cloud with team collaboration built in.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">agent orchestrator (self-hosted)</span><span class=\"src\">Show HN</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">15</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://www.zuse.sh/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Zuse</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-23</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Open-source workspace for coding agents where a single agent coordinates up to 20 Linear issues in parallel Git worktrees — ticket-to-PR orchestration across many branches at once.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">issues + worktrees</span><span class=\"src\">Show HN</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">16</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://thinkrail.ai/blog/introducing-thinkrail/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">ThinkRail</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-25</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Web-based GUI for the Pi coding agent, incubated inside JetBrains: browse sessions, review diffs and manage agent runs from the browser instead of the terminal.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">web GUI for agent</span><span class=\"src\">Hacker News</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">17</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://itsuki.app/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Itsuki</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-29</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Shared memory layer that lets Claude Code, Cursor and 24+ other AI coding tools read and write one common memory store — context stays consistent across sessions and machines.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">cross-tool agent memory</span><span class=\"src\">Show HN</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">18</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://www.opencntx.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">OpenContext</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-29</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Persistent, project-local memory for AI coding agents exposed via MCP — keeps codebase context across sessions locally instead of shipping it to a cloud memory service.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">project-local memory (MCP)</span><span class=\"src\">Hacker News</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">19</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/argus-testing/argus\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Argus</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-28</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Open-source AI agents specialized in testing web applications — generating and running end-to-end tests against your app rather than writing feature code.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">AI testing agents</span><span class=\"src\">Show HN · GitHub</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">20</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/mtford90/revue\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Revue</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-31</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Terminal TUI for reviewing large code changes — including big agent-generated diffs — one 'chapter' at a time instead of scrolling a single giant diff.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><span class=\"tag\">code review TUI</span><span class=\"src\">Show HN · GitHub</span></div>\n      </article>\n\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"col-foot\">· 20 new tools tracked ·</p>\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- ================= MIDDLE: WHITELIST UPDATES (35%) ================= -->\n  <section id=\"whitelist-updates\" class=\"col col-updates\" aria-labelledby=\"h2-updates\">\n    <div class=\"col-head\">\n      <h2 id=\"h2-updates\"><a href=\"#whitelist-updates\">Whitelist Updates</a></h2>\n      <span class=\"count\">16 items</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"cards\">\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">1</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-31-github-copilot-in-vs-code-august-2026-releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-release\">release</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-31</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">August 2026 releases roundup</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Monthly roundup consolidating all Copilot updates shipped for VS Code in August 2026 into one digest.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-31-github-copilot-in-vs-code-august-2026-releases\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release notes →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">2</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Codex CLI</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-release\">release</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-29</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">0.151.0 — MCP tool interception, plugin catalogs, sandbox hardening</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Adds a grace period for discovering tools from optional MCP servers, lets extensions inspect or replace MCP tool results before they reach the model, and validates project plugin marketplaces. Fixes preserve permission profiles across TUI turns, stop <code>/cd</code> from weakening sandbox restrictions, and prevent stale Guardian classifications from authorizing actions.</p>\n        <blockquote class=\"quote\">\"Intermittent ~55-second tail latency in codex exec on 0.150.1 and 0.151.0.\" <span class=\"qsrc\">Forum</span></blockquote>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release notes →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">3</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-28-upcoming-changes-to-github-copilot-policies-and-billing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-announcement\">announcement</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-28</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">Upcoming policy &amp; billing changes</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">From Sept 1, new Business/Enterprise signups get upfront per-seat charges; no earlier than Sept 28, Copilot Chat on github.com, mobile chat and the cloud agent merge into one unified experience with chat data retained for the life of the account. Default code review effort shifts Lite → Balanced.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-28-upcoming-changes-to-github-copilot-policies-and-billing\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Announcement →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">4</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-release\">release</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-28</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">v2.1.251 — model-switch hooks, agent fleet CLI, security fixes</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Large release (~70 entries): PreModelSwitch/PostModelSwitch hooks, live streaming of subagent tool calls to Remote Control, a spend-limit bar in <code>/usage</code>, and new attach/logs/stop/respawn/rm CLI subcommands for managing agent sessions. Also fixes symlink permission bypasses and plugin path traversal; Opus 5 becomes the Enterprise seat-based default.</p>\n        <blockquote class=\"quote\">\"Quite concerning that we are not seeing something like this more in the wild.\" <span class=\"qsrc\">HN</span></blockquote>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release notes →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">5</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-27-copilot-code-review-resolution-reasons-and-expanded-capabilities\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Copilot code review</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-feature\">feature</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-27</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">Bot PRs and large PRs now supported</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Now reviews PRs authored by bots (including Copilot cloud agent PRs, with full agentic review) and very large PRs — the 300-file/20,000-line cap is gone. A new dropdown tags resolved comments as 'Addressed', 'Won't fix' or 'Incorrect' to feed product feedback.</p>\n        <blockquote class=\"quote\">\"Peer review of changes is still important.\" <span class=\"qsrc\">HN</span></blockquote>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-27-copilot-code-review-resolution-reasons-and-expanded-capabilities\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release notes →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">6</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://www.cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cursor</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-feature\">feature</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-27</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">Cloud Agents can start from scratch, no repo needed</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">'Start from scratch' spins up a Cursor Origin repo behind the scenes — no GitHub/SCM connection required — and 'Create repo' scaffolds agent output into a repo. Live preview port-forwards the agent's environment to your browser, with Vercel publishing to a live URL.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://www.cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release notes →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">7</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Claude Code</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-feature\">feature</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-27</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">v2.1.248 adds --restricted mode</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">New <code>--restricted</code> launch mode removes code-execution tools and WebFetch, refuses bypassPermissions and ignores user/project/local settings — for untrusted or locked-down environments. Also adds per-agent prompt-cache TTL and <code>/usage-credits</code> for AWS Marketplace-billed Enterprise.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://github.com/anthropics/claude-code/blob/main/CHANGELOG.md\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release notes →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">8</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Codex CLI</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-feature\">feature</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-26</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">0.150.0 — @-mention other Codex tasks</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Reference other Codex tasks with @ mentions; agents can read, create or message tasks from the terminal. Adds a /copy picker, editable auto-titles, clickable Markdown links and permission-mode cycling — and untrusted projects can no longer inject project-level AGENTS.md instructions.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release notes →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">9</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/releases/tag/v0.57.0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gemini CLI</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-release\">release</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-25</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">v0.57.0 — silent retries, rollback, TUI hang fix</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Stable release adding context-aware silent retries and an availability TTL for capacity errors, full rollback of multi-turn requests on cancellation/abort, and execution timeouts that prevent indefinite TUI hangs.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/releases/tag/v0.57.0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release notes →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">10</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-21-the-new-github-copilot-experience-in-slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-feature\">feature</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-21</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">New agentic experience in Slack (public preview)</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Mentioning @GitHub in Slack starts agent sessions that triage/create issues, investigate failures, implement changes in a secure cloud sandbox and open PRs. Copilot can also spin up dedicated 'code channels' where teams follow plans, review diffs and steer the agent collaboratively.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-21-the-new-github-copilot-experience-in-slack\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release notes →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">11</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-21-shared-agentic-work-with-github-copilot-in-microsoft-teams\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">GitHub Copilot</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-feature\">feature</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-21</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">Shared agentic work in Microsoft Teams (public preview)</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Mention @GitHub in a Teams channel, thread or DM to start a collaborative agent session everyone can see and steer; code changes run asynchronously in a secure cloud sandbox. Sessions continue from terminal, Copilot app or IDE, and repo admins can require approval before Copilot-authored PRs merge.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://github.blog/changelog/2026-08-21-shared-agentic-work-with-github-copilot-in-microsoft-teams\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release notes →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">12</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/desktop/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Devin Desktop</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-release\">release</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-21</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">v3.8.20 (formerly Windsurf) — Agent Command Center, plan files</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Agent Command Center runs multiple agent windows simultaneously; Devin Local gains multi-root workspaces and plan mode producing a reviewable Markdown plan with an 'Implement' button, plus individually stoppable subagents. Cloud adds live streaming shell output and better session filtering.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://docs.devin.ai/desktop/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release notes →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">13</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Codex CLI</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-feature\">feature</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-20</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">0.149.0 — interactive <code>codex agents</code> dashboard, <code>codex queue</code></p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">New interactive <code>codex agents</code> dashboard to search, start, open and stop tasks with configurable shortcuts; <code>codex queue</code> messages existing local or remote sessions. Adds /cd, /pwd, /cwd, expanded Vim motions and <code>codex doctor</code> diagnostics.</p>\n        <blockquote class=\"quote\">\"Changes created by Codex had fewer comments in Ruby code. Claude is creating verbose comments and people are tired of it.\" <span class=\"qsrc\">HN</span></blockquote>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://developers.openai.com/codex/changelog/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release notes →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">14</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/releases/tag/v0.56.0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Gemini CLI</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-release\">release</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-19</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">v0.56.0 released</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Routine stable minor release with no highlighted notes; follows v0.55.1 with ongoing fixes to IDE connections and eval tooling.</p>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://github.com/google-gemini/gemini-cli/releases/tag/v0.56.0\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release notes →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">15</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://www.cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cursor</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-feature\">feature</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-19</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">Cloud Agent subscriptions, custom modes, isolated subagents, /goal</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Agents can subscribe to PRs, Slack threads or scheduled tasks and wake when events occur — auto-subscribed to their own PRs to fix CI and answer comments. Custom modes pin any skill as always-on, subagents run on isolated VMs, <code>/goal</code> sets long-lived objectives, and steering messages wait for the next tool call instead of interrupting mid-action.</p>\n        <blockquote class=\"quote\">\"Autonomous agents that 'just handle it' create more work, not less.\" <span class=\"qsrc\">Forum</span></blockquote>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://www.cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Release notes →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"idx\">16</span>\n          <h3><a href=\"https://www.cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Cursor</a></h3>\n          <span class=\"type t-announcement\">announcement</span>\n          <span class=\"date\">2026-08-17</span>\n        </div>\n        <p class=\"subtitle\">Origin code hosting launches (early beta)</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Cursor's own code-hosting service on all paid plans: Origin repos with a Codebase tab and CLI clone/push, real-time GitHub sync/mirroring, two-way PR comment and review sync, agents in every repo, and extensions for Vercel, Depot and Buildkite.</p>\n        <blockquote class=\"quote\">\"Any plans for compatibility with GitHub's APIs? … This produces some degree of lock-in.\" <span class=\"qsrc\">HN</span></blockquote>\n        <div class=\"meta\"><a class=\"notes-link\" href=\"https://www.cursor.com/changelog\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Announcement →</a></div>\n      </article>\n\n    </div>\n    <p class=\"col-foot\">· 16 tracked products updated ·</p>\n  </section>\n\n  <!-- ================= RIGHT: TECHNICAL INSIGHTS (25%) ================= -->\n  <section id=\"technical-insights\" class=\"col col-insights\" aria-labelledby=\"h2-insights\">\n    <div class=\"col-head\">\n      <h2 id=\"h2-insights\"><a href=\"#technical-insights\">Technical Insights</a></h2>\n      <span class=\"count\">38 items</span>\n    </div>\n    <div class=\"cards\">\n\n      <article class=\"card insight\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"type t-opinion\">opinion</span><span class=\"date\">2026-08-31</span></div>\n        <h3><a href=\"https://x.com/amasad\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">\"Civilizations are built with [Agent() for _ in range(100)]\"</a></h3>\n        <p class=\"author\">Amjad Masad · Twitter</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Replit's CEO: civilization-building is \"actually easy\" with a hundred agents — agent swarms, not individual developers, as the unit of software production.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card insight\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"type t-opinion\">opinion</span><span class=\"date\">2026-08-31</span></div>\n        <h3><a href=\"https://x.com/amasad\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">On the Hugging Face incident: RLVR produces increasingly weird behavior</a></h3>\n        <p class=\"author\">Amjad Masad · Twitter</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">\"RL with verifiable rewards will produce increasingly weird and surprising behavior\" — OpenAI's miss was not monitoring agent activity despite calling it a safety strategy.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card insight\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"type t-discussion\">discussion</span><span class=\"date\">2026-08-31</span></div>\n        <h3><a href=\"https://www.theverge.com/tech/986789/linux-debian-generative-ai-policy\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">Debian votes not to ban AI code from its distribution</a></h3>\n        <p class=\"author\">The Verge</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">'Responsible' AI use is allowed in contributions: generative AI is \"neither exempt from nor subject to special rules\" — a landmark governance call for AI code in critical OSS.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card insight\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"type t-discussion\">discussion</span><span class=\"date\">2026-08-31</span></div>\n        <h3><a href=\"https://www.technologyreview.com/2026/08/31/1143180/hugging-face-hack-could-indicate-cultural-issues-at-openai\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">The Hugging Face hack could indicate cultural issues at OpenAI</a></h3>\n        <p class=\"author\">MIT Technology Review</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Beyond the post-mortem: redacted risk reporting, slow disclosure, and an org increasingly organized around autonomous agent swarms.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card insight\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"type t-tutorial\">tutorial</span><span class=\"date\">2026-08-31</span></div>\n        <h3><a href=\"https://towardsdatascience.com/agentops-is-not-mlops-what-breaks-in-your-monitoring-stack-when-agents-go-to-production/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">AgentOps Is Not MLOps</a></h3>\n        <p class=\"author\">Mostafa Ibrahim · Towards Data Science</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Agents break MLOps-style monitoring: non-deterministic multi-step traces, tool-call failures and cost explosions demand traces over spans, tool-level alerting and in-production evals.</p>\n      </article>\n\n      <article class=\"card insight\">\n        <div class=\"card-head\"><span class=\"type t-discussion\">discussion</span><span class=\"date\">2026-08-31</span></div>\n        <h3><a href=\"https://news.ycombinator.com/item?id=49506519\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener\">HN (64 pts): Claude Code cuts weekly usage limits by 17%</a></h3>\n        <p class=\"author\">Hacker News community</p>\n        <p class=\"desc\">Developers debate the uni